# CT 123 (`gpu2`) — Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on ONE Radeon Pro V620. ✅ THIS IS THE SHIPPED SHAPE.
#   VMID=123 ENV_FILE=qwen38fn-gpu2.env ./install.sh      -> /etc/llamacpp-qwen38fn.env
#
# ⚠️ systemd EnvironmentFile= does NOT strip trailing inline comments — comments go on their
# own lines, never after a VAR=value.
#
# 🔴 ONE CARD IS FASTER THAN TWO, which is the counter-intuitive part. Matched pair at
# -ncmoe 34, only the device count differing: one card +20.9% at a short prompt, +24.2% at 8k,
# prefill identical. llama.cpp sends the QSA indexer's pooled rows across the inter-GPU link
# every layer (#28699, per-device fix still an open draft) — a fixed per-token penalty decode
# pays every token and prefill amortises away.
#
# ⚠️ PREFILL-BOUND, AND NOT SUITABLE FOR AN AGENT. 39 t/s prefill means an 8k prompt costs
# ~205 s before the first token. Hermes deliberately uses CT 120's qwen3.6-35b-a3b instead.
# Use this endpoint for one deep question you are willing to wait on.
#
# 📖 Every measurement and retraction behind these values is in README.md. This file carries
# only what you need to change one safely.

# 🔴 b11013 is a HARD FLOOR: the qwen4exp arch STRING is in b10678, so a grep says
# "supported", but the Vulkan hyper-connection ops only landed in #28988. b10678 cannot
# execute this model on RADV — it is NOT a rollback target. Roll back to b11013 or later.
# ⚠️ Name the TREE, not the container. This `b11018-baseline` (GNU 13.3.0, sha 32687325) is
# byte-identical to CT 120's copy of the same tree; CT 120 ALSO has `llama-b11018` (release,
# GNU 11.4.0, sha 4ac7aa75), which is what the two-card env pins.
LLAMACPP_DIR="/opt/llamacpp/b11018-baseline"

# First shard only; llama.cpp discovers 00002..00004 itself.
MODEL_PATH=/models/hf/qwen3.8-flash-next/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00004.gguf
MODEL_ALIAS=qwen3.8-flash-next

# Vision projector, +~1.1 GiB VRAM. ⚠️ Without it the server answers "image input is not
# supported" and an agent keeps working regardless — a silent failure mode already hit here.
MODEL_MMPROJ=/models/hf/qwen3.8-flash-next/mmproj-F16.gguf

MODEL_SERVER_BIND=0.0.0.0
MODEL_SERVER_PORT=1234

# All non-expert layers on GPU. Placement is MODEL_CPU_MOE below, not this.
MODEL_GPU_LAYERS="99"

# 🔴 The PLE n-gram table (~28.7 GB at Q4) to host RAM. It is a row LOOKUP, not a matmul, so
# it costs almost nothing off-GPU and is what makes Q4 reachable: 111.3 GB -> ~82.6 GB
# GPU-side. ⚠️ The tensor is `per_layer_token_embd`; `ngram_embedding` is the SAFETENSORS
# name and matches nothing in a GGUF.
MODEL_OT_OVERRIDE="per_layer_token_embd=CPU"

# 🔴 34 IS THE FLOOR FOR ONE CARD — 30.4 GiB of 32. Lower does not fit on a single device.
#   34 -> 13.01 t/s, 1.7 GiB free  <- this config     40 -> 11.40 t/s, 10.4 GiB free
#   36 -> 12.43 t/s, 4.6 GiB free                     48 -> 10.18 t/s, 23.3 GiB free
# Each +1 hands ~1.56 GB back to VRAM and moves that layer's expert read onto the memory bus.
MODEL_CPU_MOE="34"

# ⚠️ Explicit, never `auto` / `--fit on`: on RADV auto-fit over-commits and puts the KV cache
# silently in GTT — a ~12x decode collapse the startup guard does NOT catch.
MODEL_CONTEXT_LENGTH="65536"
MODEL_PARALLEL="1"

# Physical cores; SMT siblings add no memory bandwidth. ⚠️ Not 8 and not 32: 32 is contention
# (-4 to -5%), 8 wins solo by ~1% but LOSES 4.9% at four streams.
MODEL_THREADS="16"

# ⚠️ COUNTED, not checked for non-zero: a missing card does not fail a load on its own,
# llama.cpp would quietly place those layers in host RAM. 1 here, with --device below.
MODEL_EXPECTED_GPUS="1"

# Leave EMPTY. ⚠️ Never "none" or "high" — this template RAISES on exactly those two, the
# inverse of Qwen3.8-27B. The server sets --reasoning off, which neutralises it.
# MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT=

# 🔴 EMPTY on purpose: nothing to split across on one card, and passing --tensor-split with a
# single device is how you get a confusing partial placement.
MODEL_TENSOR_SPLIT=""

# auto (default) | none | mmap | mlock. llama.cpp suggests `none` at startup for CPU tensor
# overrides; measured WORSE (11.18 vs 11.74 t/s, and 31.6 GiB into GTT). Left on auto.
MODEL_LOAD_MODE=""

# Pins this server to GPU 2 alone. Appended verbatim to llama-server (word-split).
EXTRA_ARGS="--device Vulkan0"

# Measured safe HERE: 28965 MiB used of 30704 (1739 free), 241 MiB GTT, above the ~1024 MiB
# RADV floor. ⚠️ Do NOT copy to the two-card env — the same batch drops its card 2 to 877 MiB.
# The compute buffer lands on whichever card holds the heavy layers, so batch size and
# --tensor-split are coupled knobs.
MODEL_BATCH_SIZE="4096"
MODEL_UBATCH_SIZE="1024"

# 🔴 q8_0 KV is safe ONLY because the server runs --reasoning off. Hard XOR on this box:
# `reasoning off + q8_0` OR `reasoning low/medium + f16`. Mixing gives silent EMPTY replies,
# so do not relax --reasoning without reverting this to f16.
# ⚠️ --no-mmproj-offload costs 3-5x on IMAGE ENCODING only; text is unaffected.
MODEL_KV_TYPE="q8_0"
MODEL_MMPROJ_ON_CPU="true"
